[gd_scene load_steps=9 format=3 uid="uid://dyn1gvqmsa441"]

; THE MARK ONE, in the player's hands.
;
; ADS SOLVE, and it is the same three numbers for every iron-sighted weapon.
;
; ads_rotation is ZERO. The model's sight line is flat — rear aperture centre
; and front post tip both at model y 0.573 — and hud_weapon_template.gd traces
; the shot from the camera ALONG THE MUZZLE'S +X, so pitching the model to
; correct a sight picture aims the bullet off the crosshair instead. This scene
; used to carry a -0.01148 pitch and put its rounds 0.76 degrees low.
;
; ads_position.y = 0.123 / 0.26 - 0.573 = -0.099923. The Holder sits 0.123m
; under the eye and scales by 0.26, so that is the offset landing model y 0.573
; on the optical axis. Bore, post tip and aperture centre then all project to
; dead centre, which is the only arrangement where the irons and the reticle
; agree about where the bullet goes.
;
; ads_position.x puts the rear aperture 0.278m from the eye; .z = -0.4 centres
; it laterally (0.26 * -0.4 + 0.104 = 0).
;
; None of this is eyeballed any more. tools/preview_viewmodel.gd prints the
; camera-local x, y and depth of both sights; correct numbers read as zeroes.

